  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Life Chances&amp;Household Income of People with Disabilities in 8 Subcoun</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There are about 16,000 people with disabilities in Moyo District, N. Uganda needing specific assistance to have a chance of getting a job or setting up a new enterprise in a rural area recovering from a long period of armed conflict.  This project will start to work with 1,000 people with disabilities to provide rehabilitation support, training, career counselling, and acquire locally relevant vocational skills. Some 600 will get group support, loans, or intensive training to take up formal jobs or set up new businesses for themselves. Traditional attitudes to disability are harsh however, so there will be outreach and awareness raising to reduce barriers and social stigma and find partners.</narrative>
  </description>
